---
description: Build clause packages as coherent trade-offs over a linked clause graph and preserve scoped approval.
args: { request: NegotiationPackageRequest; vault: ClauseTermVault }
returns: ClauseProgramResult
uses: [clauseDesk/frameNegotiation, clauseDesk/expandGlobalTermImpact, clauseDesk/stripInternalComments, clauseDesk/preserveConditionalAcceptance, clauseDesk/bindApprovalToHash, clauseDesk/rejectUndefinedTerm, clauseWorkbench/recoverIssueMandates, clauseWorkbench/mapClauseGraph, clauseWorkbench/composeTradeoffPackages, clauseWorkbench/readRedlineConsequences, clauseWorkbench/prepareExternalOffer]
---
Bind mandate = `frameNegotiation(request, vault.negotiations)` and positions = `recoverIssueMandates(mandate, vault.negotiations, vault.evidencePages)`. Keep each party's preferred outcome, approved fallback and prohibited concession as separate authorities. Bind globalImpact = `expandGlobalTermImpact(request, vault.globalDefinitions)` before mapping the package; a changed defined term must be tested at every clause that consumes it.

Bind clauseGraph = `mapClauseGraph(mandate, positions, vault.evidencePages, globalImpact)`. Preserve direction and condition on each dependency, including definition-to-clause, exception-to-cap, remedy-to-indemnity and cross-reference edges. If a material interaction has competing readings, retain both consequences and do not use an isolated clause score to select a package.

Bind undefined = `rejectUndefinedTerm(request, vault.undefinedTermChecks)` before package comparison. Bind packages = `composeTradeoffPackages(mandate, positions, clauseGraph, vault.evidencePages, undefined)`; carry its blockers into the package set and do not compare or circulate while any introduced term is undefined. Compare materially different whole-package combinations against every hard limit and retained protection; do not combine separately permissible concessions when their interaction violates mandate. Bind conditional = `preserveConditionalAcceptance(request, vault.conditionalAcceptances)` and redlines = `readRedlineConsequences(request, packages, conditional, vault.evidencePages)`. Keep counterparty assent tied to its prerequisite and clause hash.

Bind rendering = `stripInternalComments(request, vault.commentNotes)` before any offer text is prepared. Keep the protected negotiation history apart from the external artifact, and block output if inspection detects fallback material in rendered text. Bind approval = `bindApprovalToHash(request, vault.draftApprovals)` after the exact rendered and redlined package is fixed. An approval on an earlier hash authorizes only that version. Bind offer = `prepareExternalOffer(request, packages, redlines, rendering, approval)` only when the package set has no undefined-term blockers, conditions remain explicit, no prohibited concession is present, comments are absent and approval matches the current hash. Return ClauseProgramResult with positions, dependency graph, package alternatives, redline findings, offer plan and guardrails `[globalImpact, undefined, conditional, rendering, approval]`; keep internal blockers separate from external text. `commitAllowed` is false and circulation awaits host authorization.
